, so the statement is true.","m":1,"df":"easy","tp":"Statistical statements","st":"Statistical statements","cfg":{"question_number":10,"paper_question_key":10,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"A","criterion_label":"Criterion A — Knowing and understanding","criterion_title":"Knowing and understanding","difficulty_level":"basic","marks":1,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","source":"myp4-grade9-statistics-version-c-2025-26"}},{"n":11,"t":"true_false","p":"In an unequal-width histogram, vertical bar height represents frequency density so bar area is proportional to frequency.","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In an unequal-width histogram, vertical bar height represents frequency density so bar area is proportional to frequency."}]}]},"e":"Height = frequency density = frequency ÷ class width, so area = height × width is proportional to frequency.","m":1,"df":"easy","tp":"Statistical statements","st":"Statistical statements","cfg":{"question_number":11,"paper_question_key":11,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"C","criterion_label":"Criterion C — Communicating","criterion_title":"Communicating","difficulty_level":"basic","marks":1,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","source":"myp4-grade9-statistics-version-c-2025-26"}},{"n":12,"t":"true_false","p":"Adding 5 marks to every score in a class increases both the mean $\\mu$ and standard deviation $\\sigma$ by 5.","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adding 5 marks to every score in a class increases both the mean "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\mu"}},{"type":"text","text":" and standard deviation "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\sigma"}},{"type":"text","text":" by 5."}]}]},"e":"The mean increases by 5, but the deviations from the mean — and therefore σ — are unchanged.","m":1,"df":"easy","tp":"Statistical s