mative","marking_breakdown":[{"label":"Range","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"Median","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"Mean","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"Variance","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"SD","marks":1,"focus":""}],"parts":[{"id":"range","label":"Range","prompt":"Range","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what Range is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for Range."],"unit":"cm","answer":7,"tolerance":0},{"id":"median","label":"Median","prompt":"Median","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what Median is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for Median."],"unit":"cm","answer":15,"tolerance":0},{"id":"mean","label":"Mean","prompt":"Population mean μ","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what Mean is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for Mean."],"unit":"cm","answer":15,"tolerance":0},{"id":"var","label":"Variance","prompt":"Population variance σ²","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what Variance is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for Variance."],"unit":"cm²","answer":6,"tolerance":0},{"id":"sd","label":"SD","prompt":"Population standard deviation σ (2 d.p.)","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what SD is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for SD."],"unit":"cm","answer":2.45,"tolerance":0.01}],"source":"myp4-grade9-statistics-version-c-2025-26"}},{"n":24,"t":"assess_parts","p":"Daily solar output (kWh) summary: Min = 140, $Q_1$ = 200, Median = 225, $Q_3$ = 240, Max = 315. Using the $1.5 \\times IQR$ criterion: [4]\n**IQR:**   **Lower fence:**   **Upper fence:**   **Are any values outliers? (Yes/No + value):**","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Daily solar output (kWh) summary: Min = 140, "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"Q_1"}},{"type":"text","text":" = 200, Median = 225, "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"Q_3"}},{"type":"text","text":" = 240, Max = 315. Using the "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"1.5 \\times IQR"}},{"type":"text","text":" criterion: [4]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**IQR:**   **Lower fence:**   **Upper fence:**   **Are any values outliers? (Yes/No + value):**"}]}]},"e":"IQR = 240 − 200 = 40. Lower fence = 200 − 1.5(40) = 140; upper fence = 240 + 60 = 300. The minimum 140 lies on the lower fence; the maximum 315 > 300 is an outlier.","m":4,"df":"medium","tp":"Outliers","st":"1.5 × IQR fences","cfg":{"question_number":24,"paper_question_key":24,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"D","criterion_label":"Criterion D — Applying mathematics in real-life contexts","criterion_title":"Applying mathematics in real-life contexts","difficulty_level":"intermediate","marks":4,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","marking_breakdown":[{"label":"IQR","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"Lower fence","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"Upper fence","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"Outlier decision","marks":1,"focus":""}],"parts":[{"id":"iqr","label":"IQR","prompt":"Interquartile range","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what IQR is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for IQR."],"unit":"kWh","answer":40,"tolerance":0},{"id":"low","label":"Lower fence","prompt":"Lower fence","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what Lower fence is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for Lower fence."],"unit":"kWh","answer":140,"tolerance":0},{"id":"high","label":"Upper fence","prompt":"Upper fence","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what Upper fence is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for Upper fence."],"unit":"kWh","answer":300,"tolerance":0},{"id":"out","label":"Outliers","prompt":"Are there outliers? Write Yes or No and the value.","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what Outliers is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for Outliers."],"accepted":["Yes, 315","Yes 315 kWh","Yes — 315","Yes (315)"],"keywords":[["yes"],["315"]],"minKeywordGroups":2}],"source":"myp4-grade9-statistics-version-c-2025-26"}},{"n":25,"t":"assess_parts","p":"**Complete** the missing entries in this continuous grouped table: [4]\nTime t (min)\n | Class width\n | Frequency\n | Freq. density\n\n0 ≤ t < 10\n | 10\n | 15\n | (a) ________\n\n10 ≤ t < 25\n | (b) ________\n | 36\n | (c) ________\n\n25 ≤ t < 45\n | 20\n | (d) ________\n | 0.6\n\n**(a)** Frequency density   **(b)** Class width   **(c)** Frequency density   **(d)** Frequency","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Complete** the missing entries in this continuous grouped table: [4]"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Time t (min)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Class width"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Frequency"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Freq. density"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"0 ≤ t < 10"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"10"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"15"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(a) ________"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"10 ≤ t < 25"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(b) ________"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"36"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(c) ________"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"25 ≤ t < 45"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"20"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(d) ________"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"0.6"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(a)** Frequency density   **(b)** Class width   **(c)** Frequency density   **(d)** Frequency"}]}]},"e":"(a) 15 ÷ 10 = 1.5. (b) 25 − 10 = 15. (c) 36 ÷ 15 = 2.4. (d) 0.6 × 20 = 12.","m":4,"df":"medium","tp":"Grouped tables","st":"frequency density","cfg":{"question_number":25,"paper_question_key":25,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"A","criterion_label":"Criterion A — Knowing and understanding","criterion_title":"Knowing and understanding","difficulty_level":"intermediate","marks":4,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","marking_breakdown":[{"label":"(a)","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(b)","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(c)","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(d)","marks":1,"focus":""}],"parts":[{"id":"a","label":"(a)","prompt":"Frequency density for 0 ≤ t < 10","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a) is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)."],"answer":1.5,"tolerance":0},{"id":"b","label":"(b)","prompt":"Class width for 10 ≤ t < 25","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (b) is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (b)."],"unit":"min","answer":15,"tolerance":0},{"id":"c","label":"(c)","prompt":"Frequency density for 10 ≤ t < 25","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (c) is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (c)."],"answer":2.4,"tolerance":0},{"id":"d","label":"(d)","prompt":"Frequency for 25 ≤ t < 45","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (d) is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (d)."],"answer":12,"tolerance":0}],"source":"myp4-grade9-statistics-version-c-2025-26"}},{"n":26,"t":"assess_parts","p":"Commute times: $0 \\le t < 10$ $(f=6)$, $10 \\le t < 20$ $(f=k)$, $20 \\le t < 30$ $(f=9)$. Given the estimated mean is 16 min: [3]\n$6(5) + 9(25) =$ ______  $\\Rightarrow$  $k =$ ______","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Commute times: "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"0 \\le t < 10"}},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(f=6)"}},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"10 \\le t < 20"}},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(f=k)"}},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"20 \\le t < 30"}},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(f=9)"}},{"type":"text","text":". Given the estimated mean is 16 min: [3]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"6(5) + 9(25) ="}},{"type":"text","text":" ______  "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\Rightarrow"}},{"type":"text","text":"  "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"k ="}},{"type":"text","text":" ______"}]}]},"e":"6(5) + 9(25) = 30 + 225 = 255. Then (255 + 15k)/(15 + k) = 16, so 255 + 15k = 240 + 16k and k = 15.","m":3,"df":"medium","tp":"Grouped mean","st":"unknown frequency","cfg":{"question_number":26,"paper_question_key":26,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"B","criterion_label":"Criterion B — Investigating patterns","criterion_title":"Investigating patterns","difficulty_level":"intermediate","marks":3,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"p