lass. [1]"}]}]},"e":"(a)(i) 29.5 mm and 39.5 mm. (ii) Modal class 30–39 mm (f = 20); the 25th and 26th pods lie in the same class, so the median class is 30–39 mm. (iii) Weighted total = 8(24.5)+20(34.5)+14(44.5)+8(54.5)=1 945; mean = 38.9 mm.\n(b)(i) At cumulative frequency 40, median = 12 h; at 20, Q1 = 8 h; at 60, Q3 = 16 h; IQR = 8 h. (ii) 8 students (10%).\n(c)(i) 10÷5=2.0; 25÷10=2.5; 16÷20=0.8. (ii) Heights 4.0 cm, 5.0 cm and 1.6 cm.","m":10,"df":"hard","tp":"Grouped data and cumulative frequency","st":"boundaries, modal class, mean, quartiles, frequency density","cfg":{"question_number":1,"paper_question_key":31,"paper_section":"B","myp_criterion":"A","criterion_label":"Criterion A — Knowing and understanding","criterion_title":"Knowing and understanding","difficulty_level":"challenge","marks":10,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","marking_breakdown":[{"label":"(a)(i)","marks":1,"focus":"class boundaries"},{"label":"(a)(ii)","marks":1,"focus":"modal and median class"},{"label":"(a)(iii)","marks":2,"focus":"weighted total and mean"},{"label":"(b)(i)","marks":2,"focus":"quartiles and IQR"},{"label":"(b)(ii)","marks":1,"focus":"number and percentage"},{"label":"(c)(i)","marks":2,"focus":"three frequency densities"},{"label":"(c)(ii)","marks":1,"focus":"three bar heights"}],"parts":[{"id":"a1","label":"(a)(i)","prompt":"Lower and upper boundaries of 30–39 mm","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(i) is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(i)."],"accepted":["29.5 and 39.5","29.5 mm and 39.5 mm","29.5, 39.5","29.5 to 39.5"]},{"id":"a2","label":"(a)(ii)","prompt":"Modal class and class containing the median","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(ii) is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(ii)."],"accepted":["30–39 and 30–39","30-39 mm; 30-39 mm","Both 30–39 mm","30–39 mm, 30–39 mm"],"keywords":[["30","39"]],"minKeywordGroups":1},{"id":"a3","label":"(a)(iii) total","prompt":"Weighted total using midpoints","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(iii) total is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(iii) total."],"answer":1945,"tolerance":0},{"id":"a4","label":"(a)(iii) mean","prompt":"Estimated mean pod length (1 d.p.)","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(iii) mean is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(iii) mean."],"unit":"mm","answer":38.9,"tolerance":0.05},{"id":"b1","label":"(b)(i) quartiles","prompt":"Median, Q1, Q3 and IQR of revision times","kind":"text","points":2,"hints":["Re-read what (b)(i) quartiles is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (b)(i) quartiles."],"accepted":["median 12 h, Q1 8 h, Q3 16 h, IQR 8 h","12, 8, 16, 8","Med 12, Q1 8, Q3 16, IQR 8"],"keywords":[["12"],["8"],["16"],["iqr","interquartile"]],"minKeywordGroups":4},{"id":"b3","label":"(b)(ii)","prompt":"Number and percentage revising more than 20 hours","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (b)(ii) is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (b)(ii)."],"accepted":["8 students, 10%","8 and 10%","8, 10%","8 students (10%)"]},{"id":"c1","label":"(c)(i) first two","prompt":"Frequency densities for the first two classes","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (c)(i) first two is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (c)(i) first two."],"accepted":["2.0 and 2.5","2, 2.5","2.0, 2.5"]},{"id":"c2","label":"(c)(i) third","prompt":"Frequency density for 15 ≤ t < 35","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (c)(i) third is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (c)(i) third."],"answer":0.8,"tolerance":0},{"id":"c3","label":"(c)(ii)","prompt":"Bar heights in cm for the three classes","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (c)(ii) is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (c)(ii)."],"accepted":["4, 5, 1.6","4.0, 5.0, 1.6","4 cm, 5 cm, 1.6 cm"]}],"source":"myp4-grade9-statistics-version-c-2025-26"}},{"n":32,"t":"assess_parts","p":"**QUESTION 2 · CRITERION B: INVESTIGATING PATTERNS [10 marks]**\n**(a)** Six ordered test scores are $\\{40, 42, 44, 46, 48, 50\\}$.\n**(i)** **Calculate** the mean, median and IQR of these 6 scores. [2]\n**(ii)** A seventh student scores $y = 10$. **Find** the new mean, median and IQR of all 7 scores. [2]\n**(b)** Suppose the seventh score is any value $y$ satisfying $0 \\le y \\le 40$.\n**(i)** **Write** a formula in terms of $y$ for the mean of the 7 scores. [1]\n**(ii)** **Investigate** the median and IQR for different values of $y$ in $0 \\le y \\le 40$, **state** a general rule, and **explain** mathematically why both remain invariant across this interval. [2]\n**(c)** **Compare** two 8-value datasets (in kg):\n• Set A: $\\{1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 11, 12, 13\\}$   • Set B: $\\{3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 13, 15, 17\\}$\n**(i)** **Compute** the exact mean of Set A and of Set B. [1]\n**(ii)** Group both sets into $0 \\le x < 10$ and $10 \\le x < 20$, **show** they produce the same grouped estimated mean, and **explain** why the midpoint estimate is exact for Set B but overestimates Set A. [2]","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**QUESTION 2 · CRITERION B: INVESTIGATING PATTERNS [10 marks]**"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(a)** Six ordered test scores are "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\{40, 42, 44, 46, 48, 50\\}"}},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(i)** **Calculate** the mean, median and IQR of these 6 scores. [2]\n**(ii)** A seventh student scores "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"y = 10"}},{"type":"text","text":". **Find** the new mean, median and IQR of all 7 scores. [2]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(b)** Suppose the seventh score is any value "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"y"}},{"type":"text","text":" satisfying "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"0 \\le y \\le 40"}},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(i)** **Write** a formula in terms of "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"y"}},{"type":"text","text":" for the mean of the 7 scores. [1]\n**(ii)** **Investigate** the median and IQR for different values of "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"y"}},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"0 \\le y \\le 40"}},{"type":"text","text":", **state** a general rule, and **explain** mathematically why both remain invariant across this interval. [2]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(c)** **Compare** two 8-value datasets (in kg):\n• Set A: "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\{1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 11, 12, 13\\}"}},{"type":"text","text":"   • Set B: "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\{3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 13, 15, 17\\}"}}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(i)** **Compute** the exact mean of Set A and of Set B. [1]\n**(ii)** Group both sets into "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"0 \\le x < 10"}},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"10 \\le x < 20"}},{"type":"text","text":", **show** they produce the same grouped estimated mean, and **explain** why the midpoint estimate is exact for Set B but overestimates Set A. [2]"}]}]},"e":"(a)(i) Sum 270, mean 45; median 45; Q1=42, Q3=48, IQR 6. (ii) With 10: sum 280, mean 40; median 44; Q1=40, Q3=48, IQR 8.\n(b)(i) Mean = (270+y)/7. (ii) For 0 ≤ y ≤ 40 the ordered list is y,40,42,44,46,48,50, so the median (4th) is 44, Q1 (2nd) is 40, Q3 (6th) is 48, and IQR = 8 for every such y.\n(c)(i) Means 6.0 kg and 8.75 kg. (ii) Both group to f=5 in 0–10 and f=3 in 10–20, so grouped mean = (5×5+3×15)/8 = 8.75 kg. In Set B each class mean equals its midpoint (25/5=5, 45/3=15); Set A clusters low (12/5=2.4, 36/3=12), so the midpoint estimate is too high.","m":10,"df":"hard","tp":"Investigating patterns","st":"outliers, invariance and grouped means","cfg":{"question_number":2,"paper_question_key":32,"paper_section":"B","myp_criterion":"B","criterion_label":"Criterion B — Investigating patterns","criterion_title":"Investigating patterns","difficulty_level":"challenge","marks":10,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","marking_breakdown":[{"label":"(a)(i)","marks":2,"focus":"mean and median, IQR"},{"label":"(a)(ii)","marks":2,"focus":"new mean, median and IQR"},{"label":"(b)(i)","marks":1,"focus":"formula"},{"label":"(b)(ii)","marks":2,"focus":"rule and explanation"},{"label":"(c)(i)","marks":1,"focus":"two means"},{"label":"(c)(ii)","marks":2,"focus":"grouped mean and explanation"}],"parts":[{"id":"a1","label":"(a)(i) mean","prompt":"Mean of the six scores","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(i) mean is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(i) mean."],"answer":45,"tolerance":0},{"id":"a2","label":"(a)(i) median & IQR","prompt":"Median and IQR of the six scores","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(i) median & IQR is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(i) median & IQR."],"accepted":["45 and 6","median 45, IQR 6","45, 6"]},{"id":"a3","label":"(a)(ii) mean","prompt":"New mean of all seven scores","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(ii) mean is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(ii) mean."],"answer":40,"tolerance":0},{"id":"a4","label":"(a)(ii) median & IQR","prompt":"New median and IQR of all seven scores","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(ii) median & IQR is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(ii) median & IQR."],"accepted"