t","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (c)(ii) explanation is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (c)(ii) explanation."],"accepted":["Set B class means equal the midpoints, but Set A values cluster near the lower boundaries","B''s values average to the midpoints; A''s are lower within each class"],"keywords":[["set b","b"],["midpoint","class mean"],["set a","a"],["lower","overestimate","cluster"]],"minKeywordGroups":3}],"source":"myp4-grade9-statistics-version-c-2025-26"}},{"n":33,"t":"assess_parts","p":"**QUESTION 3 · CRITERION C: COMMUNICATING [10 marks]**\n**(a)** Standing broad-jump distances (cm) of 9 athletes before and after an 8-week plyometric programme:\n• **Before:** 115, 128, 122, 131, 119, 125, 135, 124, 118\n• **After:** 129, 142, 136, 148, 133, 139, 151, 144, 128\n**(i)** **Construct** an ordered back-to-back stem-and-leaf diagram (stems 11 to 15 in the centre) with a clear dual key. [3]\n**(ii)** **State** the median and range of each group and **write** two concise statistical sentences comparing performance. [2]\n**(b)** Kofi surveyed delivery distances $d$ (km) for 50 orders: $0 \\le d < 10$ $(f=12)$, $10 \\le d < 20$ $(f=18)$, $20 \\le d < 40$ $(f=20)$, and drew the chart shown.\n\n[Figure: Kofi''s delivery-distance chart]\n**(i)** **Identify** two statistical errors in Kofi''s chart. [2]\n**(ii)** **Calculate** the frequency densities and **draw** a correctly scaled histogram on your paper. [3]","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**QUESTION 3 · CRITERION C: COMMUNICATING [10 marks]**"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(a)** Standing broad-jump distances (cm) of 9 athletes before and after an 8-week plyometric programme:\n• **Before:** 115, 128, 122, 131, 119, 125, 135, 124, 118\n• **After:** 129, 142, 136, 148, 133, 139, 151, 144, 128"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(i)** **Construct** an ordered back-to-back stem-and-leaf diagram (stems 11 to 15 in the centre) with a clear dual key. [3]\n**(ii)** **State** the median and range of each group and **write** two concise statistical sentences comparing performance. [2]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(b)** Kofi surveyed delivery distances "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"d"}},{"type":"text","text":" (km) for 50 orders: "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"0 \\le d < 10"}},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(f=12)"}},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"10 \\le d < 20"}},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(f=18)"}},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"20 \\le d < 40"}},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(f=20)"}},{"type":"text","text":", and drew the chart shown."}]},{"type":"statsBlock","attrs":{"spec":{"version":1,"chart":"bar_chart","title":"Kofi''s delivery-distance chart","xLabel":"Distance d (km)","yLabel":"Frequency","values":[],"categories":[{"id":"c0","label":"0–10","value":12},{"id":"c1","label":"10–20","value":18},{"id":"c2","label":"20–40","value":20}],"binWidth":null,"showSummary":false,"dataMode":"raw"}}},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(i)** **Identify** two statistical errors in Kofi''s chart. [2]\n**(ii)** **Calculate** the frequency densities and **draw** a correctly scaled histogram on your paper. [3]"}]}]},"e":"(a)(i) Before leaves on the left, after leaves on the right:\n9 8 5 | 11 | 8\n8 4 2 | 12 | 8 9\n5 1 | 13 | 3 6 9\n4 2 | 14 | 2 4 8\n| 15 | 1\nKey: 5 | 11 | 8 means 115 cm before and 118 cm after.\n(ii) Before median 124 cm, range 20 cm; after median 139 cm, range 23 cm. The median improved by 15 cm, indicating higher typical performance, while the range increased by 3 cm, indicating slightly greater spread.\n(b)(i) The bars have gaps and equal visual widths for continuous classes of unequal width (0–10, 10–20, 20–40); and the vertical axis plots raw frequency rather than frequency density, exaggerating the 20–40 class. (ii) Frequency densities: 12/10 = 1.2, 18/10 = 1.8, 20/20 = 1.0.","m":10,"df":"hard","tp":"Communicating statistics","st":"back-to-back stem-and-leaf, flawed histogram","cfg":{"question_number":3,"paper_question_key":33,"paper_section":"B","myp_criterion":"C","criterion_label":"Criterion C — Communicating","criterion_title":"Communicating","difficulty_level":"challenge","marks":10,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","marking_breakdown":[{"label":"(a)(i)","marks":3,"focus":"back-to-back diagram"},{"label":"(a)(ii)","marks":2,"focus":"medians, ranges and comparison"},{"label":"(b)(i)","marks":2,"focus":"two errors"},{"label":"(b)(ii)","marks":3,"focus":"frequency densities and histogram"}],"response_guidance":"Use the stem-and-leaf workspace for the back-to-back diagram. Put the Before class on the left and the After class on the right of the shared stems, and include the dual key.","response_tools":["rich_text","math","stem_leaf","statistics"],"tool_labels":["rich_text","math","stem_leaf","statistics"],"parts":[{"id":"a2","label":"(a)(ii) medians and ranges","prompt":"Median and range for each group","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(ii) medians and ranges is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(ii) medians and ranges."],"accepted":["Before 124 cm range 20 cm; after 139 cm range 23 cm","Before median 124, range 20; After median 139, range 23"],"keywords":[["before","124"],["after","139"],["20"],["23"]],"minKeywordGroups":4},{"id":"a3","label":"(a)(ii) comparison","prompt":"Two concise statistical sentences comparing performance","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a)(ii) comparison is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a)(ii) comparison."],"accepted":["The median increased by 15 cm, so typical performance improved; the range increased by 3 cm, so spread increased slightly","Median improved by 15 cm but range is 3 cm larger"],"keywords":[["median","improved","increased"],["15"],["range","spread"],["3"]],"minKeywordGroups":3},{"id":"b1","label":"(b)(i) error 1","prompt":"First statistical error in Kofi''s chart","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (b)(i) error 1 is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (b)(i) error 1."],"accepted":["Gaps between bars / equal bar widths for continuous unequal classes","The bars have gaps and equal widths although the classes are continuous and unequal"],"keywords":[["gap","equal width","width"],["continuous","class","unequal"]],"minKeywordGroups":2},{"id":"b2","label":"(b)(i) error 2","prompt":"Second statistical error in Kofi''s chart","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (b)(i) error 2 is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (b)(i) error 2."],"accepted":["Raw frequency plotted instead of frequency density","The vertical axis should be frequency density"],"keywords":[["frequency density","density"],["not frequency","raw frequency","should be"]],"minKeywordGroups":1},{"id":"b3","label":"(b)(ii) frequency densities","prompt":"Frequency densities for the three classes","kind":"text","points":2,"hints":["Re-read what (b)(ii) frequency densities is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (b)(ii) frequency densities."],"accepted":["1.2, 1.8, 1.0","1.2 1.8 1.0","1.2, 1.8 and 1.0"],"keywords":[["1.2"],["1.8"],["1.0"]],"minKeywordGroups":3}],"structured_marks":[{"id":"stem","label":"(a)(i) Back-to-back stem-and-leaf diagram","tool":"stem_leaf","points":3,"mode":"stem_leaf","expected":{"rows":[{"stem":"11","left":["9","8","5"],"right":[]},{"stem":"12","left":["8","4","2"],"right":["8","9"]},{"stem":"13","left":["5","1"],"right":["3","6","9"]},{"stem":"14","left":[],"right":["2","4","8"]},{"stem":"15","left":[],"right":["1"]}]},"tolerance":0,"part":"a3"},{"id":"hist","label":"(b)(ii) Correctly scaled histogram","tool":"statistics","points":1,"mode":"statistics","expected":{"chart":"histogram","groups":[{"from":0,"to":10,"frequency":12},{"from":10,"to":20,"frequency":18},{"from":20,"to":40,"frequency":20}]},"tolerance":0.01,"part":"b3"}],"response_default_tool":"stem_leaf","response_stem_leaf":{"starter":{"version":1,"title":"Before and after broad-jump distances (cm)","layout":"back_to_back","stemLabel":"Stem","leafLabel":"Leaf","leftLeafLabel":"Before","rightLeafLabel":"After","key":"Dual key: 5 | 11 | 8 means 115 cm before and 118 cm after","rows":[{"id":"r11","stem":"11","leaves":"","leftLeaves":"","rightLeaves":""},{"id":"r12","stem":"12","leaves":"","leftLeaves":"","rightLeaves":""},{"id":"r13","stem":"13","leaves":"","leftLeaves":"","rightLeaves":""},{"id":"r14","stem":"14","leaves":"","leftLeaves":"","rightLeaves":""},{"id":"r15","stem":"15","leaves":"","leftLeaves":"","rightLeaves":""}]}},"source":"myp4-grade9-statistics-version-c-2025-26"}},{"n":34,"t":"assess_parts","p":"**QUESTION 4 · CRITERION D: REAL-LIFE CONTEXTS [10 marks]**\n**(a)** An Allada pineapple cannery checks a population batch of 8 cans:\nNet mass x (g)\n | 398\n | 399\n | 400\n | 401\n | 402\n\nNumber of cans f\n | 1\n | 2\n | 2\n | 2\n | 1\n\nQuality control requires $399.5 \\le \\mu \\le 400.5$ g and $\\sigma \\le 1.20$ g. **Calculate** $\\mu$ and $\\sigma$ (to 2 d.p.) and **determine** whether the batch passes both rules. [4]\n**(b)** Daily solar energy generated over 30 days at a Cotonou clinic:\nOutput E (kWh)\n | 8 ≤ E < 12\n | 12 ≤ E < 16\n | 16 ≤ E < 20\n | 20 ≤ E < 24\n\nNumber of days\n | 5\n | 13\n | 9\n | 3\n\nThe clinic requires at least 450 kWh over the 30 days to run its vaccine refrigerators without grid backup. **Estimate** the total energy generated and daily mean, and **advise** the clinic director. [3]\n**(c)** A coastal weather station must choose between two sensor-battery brands (lifetimes in months) and requires at least 34 months of uninterrupted operation before scheduled maintenance:\n• Brand Alpha: $\\mu = 36.4$, $\\sigma = 0.9$, IQR = 1.4\n• Brand Beta: $\\mu = 38.0$, $\\sigma = 3.4$, IQR = 5.2\n**Recommend** one brand using both centre and spread, and **state** one real-world limitation of relying only on summary statistics. [3]","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**QUESTION 4 · CRITERION D: REAL-LIFE CONTEXTS [10 marks]**"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(a)** An Allada pineapple cannery checks a population batch of 8 cans:"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Net mass x (g)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"398"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"399"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"400"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"401"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"402"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Number of cans f"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Quality control requires "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"399.5 \\le \\mu \\le 400.5"}},{"type":"text","text":" g and "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\sigma \\le 1.20"}},{"type":"text","text":" g. **Calculate** "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\mu"}},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\sigma"}},{"type":"text","text":" (to 2 d.p.) and **determine** whether the batch passes both rules. [4]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(b)** Daily solar energy generated over 30 days at a Cotonou clinic:"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Output E (kWh)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"8 ≤ E < 12"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"12 ≤ E < 16"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"16 ≤ E < 20"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"20 ≤ E < 24"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Number of days"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"5"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"13"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"9"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"3"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The clinic requires at least 450 kWh over the 30 days to run its vaccine refrigerators without grid backup. **Estimate** the total energy generated and daily mean, and **advise** the clinic director. [3]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**(c)** A coastal weather station must choose between two sensor-battery brands (lifetimes in months) and requires at least 34 months of uninterrupted operation before scheduled maintenance:\n• Brand Alpha: "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\mu = 36.4"}},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\sigma = 0.9"}},{"type":"text","text":", IQR = 1.4\n• Brand Beta: "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\mu = 38.0"}},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\sigma = 3.4"}},{"type":"text","text":", IQR = 5.2"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommend** one brand using both centre and spread, and **state** one real-world limitation of relying only on summary statistics. [3]"}]}]},"e":"(a) Weighted sum = 398(1)+399(2)+400(2)+401(2)+402(1) = 3 200 g, so μ = 400.00 g. Squared deviations give 1(4)+2(1)+2(0)+2(1)+1(4)=12, variance 1.5 g², σ = √1.5 = 1.22 g. The mean passes, but 1.22 > 1.20, so the batch fails.\n(b) Midpoints 10, 14, 18, 22 kWh: total = 5(10)+13(14)+9(18)+3(22) = 460 kWh; daily mean = 15.33 kWh. 460 ≥ 450, so the target is met, but the margin is only 10 kWh and actual values near lower boundaries could reduce output.\n(c) Recommend Alpha: Beta has the higher mean, but its much larger spread means a substantial fraction falls below 34 months. Alpha''s small σ (μ − 2σ = 34.6 > 34) makes it more reliable. Limitation: summary statistics hide the distribution, sample size, test conditions, unit cost or the effect of coastal heat, humidity and salinity.","m":10,"df":"hard","tp":"Real-life contexts","st":"quality control, grouped energy and spread","cfg":{"question_number":4,"paper_question_key":34,"paper_section":"B","myp_criterion":"D","criterion_label":"Criterion D — Applying mathematics in real-life contexts","criterion_title":"Applying mathematics in real-life contexts","difficulty_level":"challenge","marks":10,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","marking_breakdown":[{"label":"(a) mean","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(a) variance","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(a) standard deviation","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(a) decision","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(b) total","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(b) daily mean","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(b) advice","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(c) recommendation","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(c) reason","marks":1,"focus":""},{"label":"(c) limitation","marks":1,"focus":""}],"parts":[{"id":"a1","label":"(a) mean","prompt":"Population mean μ (2 d.p.)","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a) mean is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a) mean."],"unit":"g","answer":400,"tolerance":0.005},{"id":"a2","label":"(a) variance","prompt":"Population variance σ²","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a) variance is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a) variance."],"unit":"g²","answer":1.5,"tolerance":0.005},{"id":"a3","label":"(a) standard deviation","prompt":"Population standard deviation σ (2 d.p.)","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a) standard deviation is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a) standard deviation."],"unit":"g","answer":1.22,"tolerance":0.01},{"id":"a4","label":"(a) decision","prompt":"Does the batch pass both rules?","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (a) decision is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (a) decision."],"accepted":["No, σ = 1.22 g > 1.20 g","No — standard deviation exceeds 1.20 g","Fails because σ exceeds 1.20 g"],"keywords":[["no","fail"],["1.22","1.2"],["sigma","standard deviation","σ"]],"minKeywordGroups":2},{"id":"b1","label":"(b) total","prompt":"Estimated 30-day total energy","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (b) total is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (b) total."],"unit":"kWh","answer":460,"tolerance":0},{"id":"b2","label":"(b) daily mean","prompt":"Estimated daily mean energy (2 d.p.)","kind":"numeric","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (b) daily mean is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (b) daily mean."],"unit":"kWh/day","answer":15.33,"tolerance":0.01},{"id":"b3","label":"(b) advice","prompt":"Advice to the clinic director","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (b) advice is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (b) advice."],"accepted":["The target is met (460 kWh ≥ 450 kWh), but the margin is small","Yes, 460 kWh exceeds 450 kWh; only a 10 kWh margin"],"keywords":[["meets","exceeds","target","yes"],["450"],["margin","small","close"]],"minKeywordGroups":2},{"id":"c1","label":"(c) recommendation","prompt":"Recommended brand","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (c) recommendation is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (c) recommendation."],"accepted":["Brand Alpha","Alpha"],"keywords":[["alpha"]],"minKeywordGroups":1},{"id":"c2","label":"(c) reason","prompt":"Reason using both centre and spread","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (c) reason is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (c) reason."],"accepted":["Beta has a higher mean but much larger spread, so Alpha is more reliable above 34 months","Alpha has a slightly lower mean but much smaller σ and IQR, so fewer batteries fall below 34 months"],"keywords":[["beta","higher mean"],["alpha","smaller","lower spread","sigma","iqr"],["34","reliable"]],"minKeywordGroups":2},{"id":"c3","label":"(c) limitation","prompt":"One real-world limitation of relying only on summary statistics","kind":"text","points":1,"hints":["Re-read what (c) limitation is asking you to find.","Use the data and method named in the question for (c) limitation."],"accepted":["Summary statistics hide the shape of the distribution and the test conditions","They do not show sample size, distribution shape, cost or coastal conditions"],"keywords":[["shape","distribution","sample","conditions","cost"],["hide","do not show","cannot","ignores"]],"minKeywordGroups":2}],"source":"myp4-grade9-statistics-version-c-2025-26"}}]'::jsonb) as x
